1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,803
What if every blink skipped one second?

2
00:00:02,843 --> 00:00:04,265
You step off the curb,

3
00:00:04,305 --> 00:00:06,658
blink, and the bus that was far away

4
00:00:06,698 --> 00:00:08,719
is suddenly right in your face.

5
00:00:08,759 --> 00:00:10,514
Blink again, and it's gone.

6
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:13,878
Sports get strange.

7
00:00:13,918 --> 00:00:15,534
You throw a basketball,

8
00:00:15,574 --> 00:00:17,694
blink, and miss the whole arc.

9
00:00:17,734 --> 00:00:19,638
You never see the ball fly.

10
00:00:19,678 --> 00:00:22,086
You only ever see the ball arrive,

11
00:00:22,126 --> 00:00:22,878
or fail to.

12
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:25,508
Cooking becomes risky.

13
00:00:25,548 --> 00:00:27,347
Blink, the toast is golden.

14
00:00:27,387 --> 00:00:28,777
Blink, it's charcoal.

15
00:00:28,817 --> 00:00:31,705
Blink again, and the smoke alarm is singing

16
00:00:31,745 --> 00:00:32,863
a very high note.

17
00:00:33,350 --> 00:00:35,092
So you try never to blink.

18
00:00:35,132 --> 00:00:37,765
Staring contests become your new sport.

19
00:00:37,805 --> 00:00:40,164
But your eyes dry out like raisins,

20
00:00:40,204 --> 00:00:42,906
and your best friend tells jokes just to

21
00:00:42,946 --> 00:00:43,934
make you crack.

22
00:00:45,250 --> 00:00:46,920
Do the math, hypothetically.

23
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:50,583
About fifteen blinks a minute means fifteen seconds skipped.

24
00:00:50,623 --> 00:00:52,842
That's a quarter of your waking life,

25
00:00:52,882 --> 00:00:55,162
gone before you even finish breakfast.

26
00:00:55,650 --> 00:00:59,446
At your birthday, you blink while blowing out the candles.

27
00:00:59,486 --> 00:01:00,902
The party jumps ahead.

28
00:01:00,942 --> 00:01:02,026
The cake is gone,

29
00:01:02,066 --> 00:01:03,746
the balloons are drooping,

30
00:01:03,786 --> 00:01:06,127
and everyone has politely gone home.

31
00:01:06,850 --> 00:01:08,181
But here's the twist.

32
00:01:08,221 --> 00:01:10,791
A night of sleep is just one long blink.

33
00:01:10,831 --> 00:01:13,336
You'd wake up exactly one second later,

34
00:01:13,376 --> 00:01:16,077
rested, and the world would not have moved

35
00:01:16,117 --> 00:01:16,730
on at all.

36
00:01:19,150 --> 00:01:20,561
So you sit on a bench,

37
00:01:20,601 --> 00:01:23,133
close your eyes, and let the whole city

38
00:01:23,173 --> 00:01:24,980
stand still for a heartbeat.

39
00:01:25,020 --> 00:01:26,233
When you open them,

40
00:01:26,273 --> 00:01:28,805
the sunset has painted everything gold.

41
00:01:28,845 --> 00:01:29,201
Blink.
